### The business model — mandatory rules

There are two separate payments.

Payment 1 — Booking-confirmation fee

Paid to the platform

The customer pays a small fee through the app before the appointment is confirmed. The backend verifies successful payment before confirming the booking.

Payment 2 — Barber's service charge

Paid directly to the barber

Once the service is finished, the customer pays the barber using UPI or cash. The platform records the declared payment status but does not automatically receive this money.

Example calculation:

| Item                                         | Amount |
| -------------------------------------------- | ------ |
| Haircut                                      | ₹300   |
| Beard trim                                   | ₹150   |
| Hair wash                                    | ₹100   |
| Total service charges payable to barber      | ₹550   |
| Booking-confirmation fee payable to platform | ₹30    |
| Total customer cost                          | ₹580   |

The ₹30 is not subtracted from the ₹550 unless you deliberately change the business model. Display both amounts separately throughout the booking.

