| Booking confirmed       | Confirmation and receipt     | Confirmed appointment     | Dashboard update    |
| Barber rejects request  | Reassignment/status update   | Confirmation of rejection | Optional exception  |
| Booking reassigned      | New barber details           | New assignment            | Audit event         |
| Appointment approaching | Reminder                     | Reminder                  | Optional exception  |
| Barber on the way       | Travel update                | Status confirmation       | —                   |
| Barber arrives          | Arrival notification         | Status confirmation       | —                   |
| Service completed       | Completion and review prompt | Completion confirmation   | Dashboard update    |
| Booking fee fails       | Retry/status message         | No false confirmation     | Payment exception   |
| Refund changes state    | Refund status                | Policy-dependent update   | Refund log          |
| Direct payment disputed | Dispute reference            | Dispute reference         | Investigation alert |
| Booking cancelled       | Cancellation details         | Cancellation details      | Audit record        |

Recommended delivery channels:

- Push notifications using a service such as Firebase Cloud Messaging.
- SMS for essential updates where necessary.
- Email receipts and account communications where configured.
- In-app notifications as the durable record of important events.

Notifications should be generated from backend events and retried safely. A failed notification must not reverse a successfully confirmed booking.

# 12. Security, privacy, and fraud prevention

These requirements are essential because the app handles customer addresses, home visits, accounts, and payments.

## Authentication and access

- Use secure authentication and session expiration.
- Verify authorization on every protected endpoint.
- Enforce role-based access on the server.
- A customer can access only their own bookings and addresses.
- A barber can access only bookings assigned to them, subject to booking-stage rules.
- An admin can perform only permitted administrative actions.
- Protect administrative accounts with stronger authentication.
- Rate-limit OTP requests, logins, and sensitive endpoints.
- Revoke compromised sessions.

## Customer and location privacy

- Collect only necessary location information.
- Ask for permission at the point where it is needed.
- Keep full customer addresses hidden from unassigned barbers.
- Reveal an address only when the booking workflow authorizes it.
- Avoid exposing exact home locations in public barber search.
- Limit how long location data is retained.
- Secure document uploads and customer support attachments.
- Publish a clear privacy policy and account-deletion process.

## Payment safety

- Do not store raw card data.
- Use the payment provider's secure checkout.
- Keep gateway secrets on the server.
- Verify webhook signatures.
- Verify amount and currency.
- Deduplicate repeated webhook events.
- Keep an auditable refund history.
- Do not trust payment screenshots as automatic proof.
- Clearly distinguish platform payments from direct barber payments.

## Operational safety

- Provide a way to report misconduct or unsafe situations.
- Maintain appointment and status-change history.
- Avoid publishing personal contact details unnecessarily.
- Consider identity verification for barbers.
- Provide customer and barber support for emergencies.
- Do not expose a customer's address to every barber in the area.

## Reliability and data recovery

- Automatic database backups.
- Tested restoration procedures.
- Error tracking and server logs.
- Monitoring for failed payments and stuck bookings.
- Retry queues for notifications and webhooks.
- Safe recovery when an app closes mid-booking.
- Database migrations and versioned API contracts.

# 13. Recommended technical architecture

A practical architecture is an Android app, a backend API, a relational database, and a separate admin web dashboard.

Android application

Customer and barber experiences

Backend API and business logic

