| Error monitoring    | Crash reporting and backend monitoring                                    | Diagnose production failures                          |

You do not have to use this exact stack. The essential requirement is that booking, scheduling, and payment decisions happen securely on the backend.

## 13.1 Background jobs the backend needs

- Expire abandoned slot holds.
- Expire unanswered barber requests.
- Send upcoming appointment reminders.
- Retry failed notification delivery.
- Process payment webhooks safely.
- Check for payments stuck in pending status.
- Process eligible refunds.
- Flag incomplete or contradictory booking states.
- Generate daily/weekly operational summaries.
- Purge or anonymize data according to the retention policy.

These jobs must be idempotent so that retrying one does not accidentally charge twice, refund twice, or send contradictory booking updates.

# 14. Business rules the developer must implement

Use this as a functional acceptance checklist.

## Implementation checklist

0/28 checked

Accounts

Only approved, active barbers can receive assignments.

Customers cannot access another customer's bookings or saved addresses.

Barbers cannot access unassigned customer addresses.

Admin overrides require permission and an audit reason.

Services and prices

Only active services can be booked.

Every selected service must be offered by the assigned barber.

Prices and duration are snapshotted at booking time.

Added services require customer approval before the final price changes.

Scheduling

No overlapping confirmed appointments or active holds for the same barber.

A slot must fit service duration, working hours, and travel buffer.

Expired holds release their slots.

A reassignment must validate the replacement barber's availability.

Booking fee

A booking fee is confirmed only after server-side verification.

Duplicate payment callbacks cannot duplicate a transaction.

A failed or pending payment cannot be treated as paid.

Successful payment with failed booking triggers recovery or refund handling.

Direct payment

The barber's service amount is separate from the platform fee.

The barber records the actual amount and payment method.

Customer confirmation or dispute is recorded independently.

Direct payment declarations are not reported as platform-collected revenue.

Cancellation and support

Cancellation eligibility is checked against the saved policy.

Refund status remains pending until confirmed by the provider.

Disputes preserve the original records.

Every resolution is recorded and communicated to the parties.

Reliability

Booking creation is safe against simultaneous requests.

Critical operations use database transactions.

Money uses integer minor units and a defined currency.

All critical state transitions have timestamps and audit events.

